# Build a Production-Oriented Web-Based Employee Attendance and Task Management System

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, security engineer, UI/UX designer, and product developer.

Build a functional, responsive, Persian-first employee attendance, workforce scheduling, and task management web application for Toranj Laboratory.

This must be a working application with real authentication, persistent database storage, server-side business logic, authorization, and functional user interfaces. Do not create only a visual prototype or static dashboard.

## 1. Product objectives

The application must:
- Record employee check-in and check-out.
- Verify attendance location using browser GPS according to per-employee policies.
- Allow administrators to assign individual work schedules.
- Calculate attendance, lateness, early departure, actual working time, approved overtime, absences, leave, and missions.
- Manage tasks assigned between employees and managers.
- Provide a focused management approval inbox.
- Provide accurate attendance reports and monthly payroll-oriented summaries.
- Support mobile phones, tablets, and desktop browsers.
- Be deployable as a secure web application and eventually accessible through app.nexahealth.ir.

Do not integrate laboratory specimen tracking, patient records, test orders, test results, or sample collection workflows. This application is exclusively for EMPLOYEE attendance and workforce management.

## 2. Technology architecture

Use a practical, maintainable full-stack architecture.

Preferred approach:
- React + TypeScript frontend.
- Node.js server-side backend, using the supported full-stack runtime.
